  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to maintain a gradual increase in tiger numbers across the Barandabhar Corridor Forest while maintaining harmony with local people. This will be done by: 1) placing barbed wire fencing in Simal Dhap and Gadhas forest area to maintain natural regeneration and protect the forest area from encroachment; 2) manually removing invasive species in Gundre Mandre Chour (grassland patches); 3) utilizing bio-fencing to protect farmlands; 4) enhancing water retaining capacity in existing water holes; 5) carrying out interaction workshops with community forest user groups and women groups on tiger conservation; 6) providing basic nature guide training to local youths; 7) forming and mobilizing two Community Based Anti-Poaching Units; 8) promoting Cassava farming; 9) providing training on sewing and tailoring for Chepang women; 10) preparing a tiger conservation poster in the local language; 11) conducting conservation education sessions at schools; 12) constructing demonstration bio-gas plants; 13) mobility support for anti-poaching team; 14) conducting a tiger camera trap survey; and 15) conducting a line transect survey for prey. ..&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
